A||||14||88formula||For those with FOCOA headers I need your opinions ||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||01-21-2001||02:19 AM||||For those with the FOCOA headers I need to know if you felt a difference over your manifolds when you installed them. I have a 3.4-liter engine and am contemplating purchasing these headers for my engine.<P><BR>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||GWMORGAN||01-21-2001||08:36 AM||||Had mine installed about a month ago. Revs freely and gets up to red line more quickly. Punch the accel. at crusing speeds and she literally takes off. Also pulls stronger in the upper rpms.<BR>Worth the investment (IMHO)||||reg||14
Z||000002||fierosound||01-21-2001||01:43 PM||||You asked the same question in November...     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR> <P><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006541.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006541.html</A> <P>My answer is still the same...<P><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/headers.jpg">     <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 01-21-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000003||88formula||01-21-2001||02:10 PM||||Fierosound why do you have to have such a good memory (jk)? I know I asked the same question in November but I was hoping that there were some new guys here with some different opinions. I usually check things to death before I make a decision especially when I'm about to plant down $800 on a set of  coated headers, which would cost only $250 or less for a comparable set for a small block Chevy. <P>I was wondering how different the roller camshaft is in your motor compared to the hydraulic flat tappet camshaft in my 3.4-liter engine. I know you must be making more toque than the hydraulic flat tappet camshaft makes. Can you give me the camshaft specifications for your camshaft so I could compare them? Since I’m on the subject of your car did you get any performance numbers for you fiero from a track or G-tech? How do you like your engine now that you have had a couple of months to brake it in?<P>Thanks for the reply GWMORGAN. That is the kind of feedback I was looking for. I assume you have a stock 2.8-liter engine.<P>Thanks guys.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||01-21-2001||02:11 PM||||Forgot the signature again and I wanted to say man I love that picture.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||01-21-2001||03:03 PM||||The way I see it is that while headers might look nice ported manifolds accomplish basically the same thing for about 1/8th of the price of headers.  You can spend all the money you save on other performance stuff that the guys with headers can't afford....<P><BR>your choice<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||01-21-2001||03:41 PM||||I would have to disagree with the performanace level of headers compared to ported manifolds. I have ported manifolds and the performance gains while impressive for the amount of money invested (I did them myself so it was free!) is still not as impressive as the flow capabablities of headers. I have driven Fieros with headers and have been very impressed with the improved response even compared to my manifolds.<P>At the same time of thinking of the price of headers compared to headers of a small block chevy, one must remember that you are not buying just two headers but the crossover piece as well. Three pieces will cost a little more than two. <P>Although I do not know of anyone who has had the resources to pit FOCOA headers against Chris West's West Coast Fieros Headers "head to head" so to speak, on the dyno I would be stunned if they both did not do better than a ported manifold engine on the same level on the same dyno.<P>Had I the money, I would go headers in a heartbeat.||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||01-21-2001||06:01 PM||||Good info WKDFIRO. <P>Hey fierosound can you give me those camshaft specifications.<P>Thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierosound||01-21-2001||06:46 PM||||88<P>I've never been able to get the camshaft specs from GM... sorry||||reg||10
Z||000009||1FST2M6||01-21-2001||07:12 PM||||find a dyno.. dyno you car NOW and after your header install.. if you want a deal on the dyno runs let me know...  but DON"T install them till you dyno the car PLEASE! <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno.jpg">  <P>long tube headers from cwest co. weren't worth the $ on a stock interanls 2.8. the loss in torque was was more noticable than the increase in HP.<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 01-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||88formula||01-21-2001||09:59 PM||||Dam no camshaft specifications. That really stinks. <P>1FAST2M6 the engine that the headers are going into is a 3.4-liter Camaro engine that I am building up that is much like Fierosounds engine. It has not been installed into the car yet and the block and heads are still at the machine shop. I don't have a way of having the car dynoed unless I install the ported manifolds now and have the car dynoed, then get the FOCOA headers and have it dynoed again. I live in Massachusetts so how would you be able to hook me up with a dynamometer?<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
